{"parentUuid":"a31e6896-1709-47b2-89d7-07b21ab45e49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01E4BWqrL6tve6p4BWrof9FU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean build. Here's exactly what changed:\n\n**`compressImage` utility** (added once, used everywhere):\n- Creates a canvas, draws the image scaled to max 800px on the longest side\n- Exports as JPEG at quality 0.7\n- Returns a new `File` — if canvas fails for any reason, falls back to the original file\n\n**Camera page reload fix** — removed `capture=\"environment\"` from two inputs:\n- `ProfilePhotoUpload` component (covers cover photo, avatar, pesticide cert, UPI QR upload buttons)\n- `ProduceListingForm` \"Take Photo\" button\n\nWithout `capture`, Android shows its standard OS file picker which lists \"Camera\" and \"Files\" as options. The user still taps camera and takes a photo, but the OS picker stays within the browser sandbox — no page navigation, no reload, React state is preserved. The camera emoji label still signals the intent clearly.\n\n**Compression applied in all 3 upload paths:**\n- `handlePickFile` (profile modal) — now async, compresses before setting preview/file state\n- `handlePickImage` (produce listing form) — now async, compresses before setting preview/file state\n- `handlePick` (farm gallery) — compresses before upload, path suffix hardcoded to `.jpg` to match the output format\n\nA typical 12MP camera photo (~6MB) will compress down to roughly 80–150KB before upload, cutting mobile memory usage by ~40× and upload time from ~10s to under 1s on 4G."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":505,"cache_read_input_tokens":120337,"output_tokens":352,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":505,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterati