{"parentUuid":"5e54b58a-59b7-44b2-93fe-e21599d5bb42","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Mrv1GvB5JrT3aViPRsEqZX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean build. Here's what changed and why each piece matters:\n\n**`dropUp` state** — tracks whether to open the dropdown upward or downward. Starts `false` (opens down by default).\n\n**`inputRef`** — attached to the `<input>` so the effect can measure its position in the viewport at any moment.\n\n**`visualViewport` effect** — fires on every `resize` and `scroll` of the visual viewport (both happen when the software keyboard opens/closes or the user scrolls). It reads:\n```\nspaceBelow = vv.height + vv.offsetTop - rect.bottom\n```\n`vv.height` is the keyboard-excluded visible height. `vv.offsetTop` accounts for any viewport panning (iOS Safari can pan the viewport). `rect.bottom` is where the input ends in screen coordinates. If the gap left below the input is under 220px — not enough to comfortably show even 3 results — it sets `dropUp = true`.\n\n**Dropdown and no-results panel** — both swap `top-full mt-1` for `bottom-full mb-1` when `dropUp` is true. `bottom-full` positions the panel flush with the top edge of the input, growing upward. The `max-h-64` cap (256px) keeps it within the modal space above the input.\n\nThis fixes both usages automatically — the consumer page location bottom sheet and the farmer dashboard profile modal — since the fix lives in the shared component."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":136559,"output_tokens":341,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":136559,"cache_creation_inpu