{"parentUuid":"b90116d3-71bb-49fe-af86-fa19041b5ebe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_018vQtdPHWM6SfrWqR1ykqJ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's how the one-review-per-consumer rule is enforced at two layers:\n\n**Client (localStorage gate — instant, no network):**\n- On tab mount, checks `yff_reviewed_<farmerId>` in localStorage. If found, the \"Write a Review\" button is replaced with the ⭐ success state immediately — the form never appears.\n- On successful submit, writes that key so the same browser/device can't submit again.\n\n**Server (phone-based gate — catches other devices/browsers):**\n- `reviewer_phone` (10-digit normalized) is now sent with every submission.\n- Before inserting, the API queries `reviews` for the same `farmer_id` + `reviewer_phone`. If a row already exists, it returns `409 already_reviewed` without inserting.\n- The client handles the 409 by also writing the localStorage key and showing the success state, so the UI stays consistent.\n- `reviewer_phone` is included in the insert payload so future checks work — this requires a `reviewer_phone` column in the `reviews` table. If the column doesn't exist yet you'll need to add it via Supabase dashboard: `ALTER TABLE reviews ADD COLUMN reviewer_phone text;`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":142,"cache_read_input_tokens":162378,"output_tokens":281,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":142,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":281,"cache_read_input_tokens":162378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":142},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CajC4tgKGJ